BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Quillfeather) Tj T* () Tj T* (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY) Tj T* () Tj T* (Quillfeather Inc. is a registered C Corporation founded by three students at our university. We) Tj T* (make an innovative handwriting practice notebook with a sensor pen and a companion app that) Tj T* (helps elementary school children improve their penmanship and keeps parents informed about) Tj T* (progress. This document gives an overview of our problem, solution, market, business model,) Tj T* (competition, team, milestones and what we are asking the competition for.) Tj T* () Tj T* (THE PROBLEM) Tj T* () Tj T* (Handwriting is a foundational skill for children in the early grades. Studies that we have read) Tj T* (suggests handwriting is linked to reading, spelling and idea generation, though we admit the) Tj T* (research is mixed on how strong the link is. Despite this, teachers in many schools have less) Tj T* (and less classroom time for penmanship, because of testing, tablets and a crowded curriculum.) Tj T* (Parents often want to help at home but they do not know what good handwriting looks like at) Tj T* (each grade level, they cannot tell if the child is forming letters the right way \(for example) Tj T* (starting a letter from the bottom instead of the top\), and worksheets give no feedback when the) Tj T* (parent isn't sitting next to the child. In our early interviews with about twenty parents and) Tj T* (four teachers, most said they worried about handwriting but had no good tool, and several said) Tj T* (they simply gave up on practice at home because it turned into arguments.) Tj T* () Tj T* (OUR SOLUTION) Tj T* () Tj T* (Quillfeather is a system of three parts working together. First is a notebook with pages) Tj T* (printed with guided letter and word exercises designed around common grade level standards.) Tj T* (Second is a sensor pen that looks and feels like a normal chunky pencil-style pen but contains) Tj T* (motion and pressure sensors and a small chip that records how each letter is written. Third is) Tj T* (a companion app that receives the data by Bluetooth and turns it into feedback. While the child) Tj T* (writes, the app shows encouraging prompts and small games, and flags things like wrong stroke) Tj T* (direction, uneven size, or pressing too hard. After each session it saves a record, and every) Tj T* (week the parent gets a progress report showing practice time, areas improving, and what to work) Tj T* (on next. We believe this takes the guessing out of home practice and makes it more fun for) Tj T* (kids, which they asked for in our testing.) Tj T* () Tj T* (MARKET) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are roughly 4 to 5 million children in each elementary grade in the United States, so) Tj T* (around 25 million children in grades K through 5. Our initial target is children in grades 1) Tj T* (through 3, about 12 million, whose families spend money on educational supplies, workbooks and) Tj T* (learning apps. If just 1 percent of these children's families bought one kit that would be over) Tj T* (100,000 customers, which at our planned price is a meaningful business. We recognise that this) Tj T* (is a top down estimate and we have not yet done a detailed bottom up analysis of how many) Tj T* (families will actually pay for a device for handwriting. Secondary markets we may look at later) Tj T* (include schools, tutors, occupational therapists and homeschool groups, as well as) Tj T* (international markets.) Tj T* () Tj T* (BUSINESS MODEL) Tj T* () Tj T* (We make money in three ways. The starter kit, which includes the sensor pen, one notebook and) Tj T* (app access, sells for 49 dollars. Refill notebooks sell for 12 dollars for a pack of two.) Tj T* (Parents can also subscribe to the premium app features, such as detailed reports and multiple) Tj T* (children profiles, for 5 dollars per month. Our estimated cost to make the kit is currently) Tj T* (around 21 dollars at small volumes, which we think will come down with larger orders, and) Tj T* (refills cost about 4 dollars to print. We plan to sell mainly through our website and online) Tj T* (marketplaces first, then later through retailers and school supply channels. Our customer) Tj T* (acquisition plan relies on social media, parent bloggers, and teacher word of mouth, although) Tj T* (we haven't yet tested paid advertising so we do not know our real acquisition costs.) Tj T* () Tj ET
endstream
