BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (COMPETITION) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are many ways parents help children with handwriting. Traditional workbooks and) Tj T* (worksheets are cheap but give no feedback. Several handwriting apps for tablets exist where) Tj T* (children trace letters with a finger or stylus, but these keep children on screens and do not) Tj T* (work with real paper, and many do not give parent reporting. There are also general smart pens) Tj T* (aimed at adults for note taking and digitizing, which are more expensive and not designed for) Tj T* (children's learning. Our advantage is that children write on real paper, with immediate) Tj T* (feedback, in a product designed for kids and reporting designed for parents. We know that) Tj T* (larger companies could copy our idea if it works, and our main protection right now is speed) Tj T* (and the design of our feedback engine, for which we have not yet filed a patent but are) Tj T* (considering it.) Tj T* () Tj T* (TEAM) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marisol Tran-Okafor is our CEO, a senior studying business with a minor in education, who ran) Tj T* (the parent and teacher interviews and leads sales and partnerships. Dev Aldenhoven is our CTO,) Tj T* (a computer engineering student who designed the pen electronics and the first version of the) Tj T* (firmware. Priya Sandoval-Reyes is our head of product and software, studying computer science,) Tj T* (who built the app and the stroke analysis. We do not yet have anyone with deep experience in) Tj T* (manufacturing at scale or in childrens education product compliance, and we are looking for) Tj T* (advisors in these areas.) Tj T* () Tj T* (MILESTONES AND FINANCIALS) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have defined the core concept, built a working prototype of the pen, notebook and) Tj T* (app, and incorporated the company as a C Corp. We have placed the prototype with 14 families in) Tj T* (a first pilot, and children used it for about six weeks on average. In the pilot, parents) Tj T* (reported that they liked the weekly reports, though a few said the pen was a bit heavy and that) Tj T* (Bluetooth pairing was annoying. One customer has paid us 49 dollars for a unit, which is our) Tj T* (first revenue, and three more families have said they would buy but have not yet. We have spent) Tj T* (approximately 6,800 dollars so far, funded by the founders and a small university grant. We) Tj T* (have a website with a waitlist. Over the next twelve months we project selling about 1,500) Tj T* (kits, and revenue of roughly 100,000 dollars including refills and subscriptions, though these) Tj T* (numbers are early estimates and depend heavily on whether we can fix the pen and get cheaper) Tj T* (manufacturing.) Tj T* () Tj T* (WHAT WE ARE ASKING FOR) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to this competition to win prize funding, which we would use to produce a) Tj T* (better second version of the pen that is lighter and pairs more easily, to make a first) Tj T* (production run of around 500 units, to run a bigger pilot with at least 60 families and two) Tj T* (classrooms, and to pay for legal help on safety testing for childrens products and a possible) Tj T* (patent filing. Beyond money, we would value mentorship from judges with experience in hardware,) Tj T* (childrens products and consumer marketing, and introductions to manufacturers and to schools.) Tj T* (We believe Quillfeather is a real opportunity to help children with an important skill and we) Tj T* (thank the judges for considering our application.) Tj ET
endstream
